3. V04 COHERENT NEGATIVE-CONTROL REVIEW

R1: hostile_13 constructs a fresh equivalent wrapper and rebuilt parent,
aggregate validation and projection; its equal control validates and renders
identically. Distinct wrong decision (row033) and wrong source artifact cases
avoid duplicate-decision masking. The report checks the independent route
binding. A foreign transaction is rejected at the actual parent builder with
multiroot_transaction_mismatch; no impossible valid parent is demanded.

R2: the reconstruction helper rebinds affected container aliases and executes
all affected public validators. A changed revocation candidate produces the
actual revocation_root_candidate_mismatch, proving Root/candidate coherence,
not observation-equality branch coverage. A separate publicly valid changed
observation with a new evaluation time/identity preserves its source artifact
but breaks row130's reference. Its equivalent-observation control detects
incidental alias failures. These are distinct coverage claims.

R3: hostile_14 changes the retained/supplied row173 locator from154 to145 and
rebuilds both forward and reverse evidence. The committed expected map digest
does not change. Rejection concerns the derived unauthorized source map, not
stale self-reported graph metadata. Its fresh equivalent binding control is
positive. A separately revived eligibility carrier obtains an authentic
negative public inspection result; this is not an invented adapter exception.

R4: typed DRS, router, child, registry and MultiRoot negatives use actual public
validators. Router/child/MultiRoot identities are rebuilt when applicable.
DRS non-authority is checked before its conditional ID rule. Delta's builder
rejects forbidden nonzero counts with g2e_zero_operation_boundary_violated.
These establish bounded typed laws; summary count poisons separately establish
report consistency. No authority field absent from a public type is invented.

These source findings are STATIC inspection corroborated by the recorded full
committed focused run. This audit does not claim newly observed trace lines.
The existing V04 external trace is accepted historical review input, not a new
